      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Haemodynamic effects in 10 multi-injured patients were registered after a bolus injection of 20 mg fluphenazin-dihydrochloride (Dapotum acutum; Fa. Heyden). Favourable results were seen in pre- and afterload. Parameters such as TTI, TTIB, CE and TI, characterising myocardial oxygen consumption, were also influenced positively. A reduction of mean arterial pressure can be avoided by administering slowly increasing volume and, occasionally, catecholamines. By use of modern monitoring in ICV, thus drug seems to be free from risk."},
